__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PRIVACY_POLICY_EN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});var o=r(d[0]);const t={title:'Privacy policy',meta:'In force from 5 November 2026 \xb7 iOS and Android apps',summaryTitle:'In short',summaryChips:['No sign-up','No ads','No tracking','Nothing sold'],summary:'Tult works without signing up. Your players, games and statistics are kept on your phone. A copy of your games is also kept online, so your friends find them in their statistics and you find yours on another phone. Only your profile photo is shown to your friends: your game photos stay on your phone. A live tournament can be seen by anyone who has its code.',sections:[{title:'Who publishes the app',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['Tult is published by Maxime Lemaitre, in France, who is responsible for the processing described here. For any question about this policy: ',{email:o.CONTACT_EMAIL},'.']}]},{title:'What is saved on your phone',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['To work, the app keeps the following information in its private storage, on your device:']},{kind:'table',head:['Data','Why'],rows:[['Player profiles: name or nickname, colour, emoji, friend code, optional photo','Show the players during games and follow their progress'],['Games, scores, throws, solo challenges, tournaments and multi-game nights (with their place and team names, if you enter them)','Count the points, resume a game, keep the history'],['Photos taken during or at the end of a game, if you take any','Keep them with the game, in the history'],['Calculated statistics (averages, success rates, rankings)','Show the summaries and progress charts'],['Settings (language, voice announcements, sounds, vibrations, scale of the darts ratings)','Remember your preferences'],['Date of your last tip, if you left one','Thank you for your support']]},{kind:'paragraph',spans:['Only the information described in the next part is sent online. The app includes no usage analytics, advertising, tracking or crash reporting tool.']}]},{title:'What is kept online',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['On first launch, the app creates an anonymous account for your phone, without asking for a name or an address. It uses it to keep the following information online:']},{kind:'table',head:['Data','Why'],rows:[['Account: a technical identifier, and your email address or Google account if you choose to link your account','Recognise you, and let you find your data on another phone'],['Profile: the player you chose as yourself, with their name, colour, emoji and friend code','Let your friends find you and add you to their games'],['Profile photo: the one of the player you chose as yourself, if you set one, reduced to 256 \xd7 256 pixels','Show it to your friends'],['Players in your games: name, colour and emoji, without photos','Show their names in shared games'],['Finished or abandoned games, tournaments and multi-game nights: game, settings, players, scores, throws, points scale, dates and place if you enter it, without photos or stars','Count each game in the statistics of the players who have an account, and find it on another phone'],['Friends, guest links, and games you remove from your statistics','Make friends work, let guests find their games, and \xab Remove from my stats \xbb'],['Live tournaments and multi-game nights you run (premium option): name, place if you enter it, team and player names, colours, emojis, matches, events, courts, scores and points, without photos','Show them on the big screen and on the participants\u2019 page'],['Premium option, if you have it: its end date','Unlock live tournaments']]},{kind:'paragraph',spans:['A game only enters a person\u2019s statistics if whoever recorded it added them with their friend code or QR code, or if they confirmed being one of that phone\u2019s guests. Everyone only sees the games they played in, along with their friends and their profiles. Exchanges with the server are encrypted. Game photos and other players\u2019 photos, solo challenges, settings and backups only stay on your phone.']}]},{title:'Service providers',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['For this online data, Tult uses service providers who act on its behalf and on its instructions:']},{kind:'list',items:[[{bold:'Supabase'},' (Supabase Inc.) hosts the database and manages the accounts.'],[{bold:'Resend'},' (Resend Inc.) sends the email containing your sign-in code, if you link your account with an email address. It receives your address and that code.'],[{bold:'Google'},' identifies you if you choose to sign in with Google, under its own privacy policy. Tult then receives your email address.'],[{bold:'Netlify'},' (Netlify Inc.) hosts the tult.app website, including the live tournament pages. Like any host, it receives the IP address of the visitors of these pages.']]},{kind:'paragraph',spans:['These companies are based in the United States. Transfers of data outside the European Union are covered by the European Commission\u2019s standard contractual clauses. No data is sold or used for advertising.']}]},{title:'Legal basis',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['This processing is needed to provide the service you use: count your games, share them with the players concerned and let you find them again (Article 6(1)(b) of the GDPR).']}]},{title:'Permissions requested',blocks:[{kind:'list',items:[[{bold:'Camera'},': to scan a QR code and, if you wish, take an avatar photo or photos during and at the end of a game.'],[{bold:'Photos'},': to pick an avatar image or a souvenir photo from your gallery.']]},{kind:'paragraph',spans:['These permissions are only requested when you use the feature concerned. You can refuse or withdraw them at any time in your phone\u2019s settings; the rest of the app keeps working. The images you pick are copied into the app; they only leave it in a backup you create yourself, except your profile photo, shown to your friends in a reduced version.']}]},{title:'What you choose to share',blocks:[{kind:'list',items:[[{bold:'QR code, friend code and link'},': your QR code contains your name, colour, emoji, friend code and account identifier, never your photo. A guest\u2019s contains their name, colour and emoji. The link that lets a guest find their games works only once and expires after 7 days.'],[{bold:'Results card'},': when you share an image at the end of a game or tournament, it shows the names, scores and ratings, but not the players\u2019 photos. It goes through your phone\u2019s share menu. The app or service you choose (messaging, social network\u2026) then applies its own privacy policy.'],[{bold:'Game photos'},': the photos taken during or at the end of a game stay on your phone. They only leave it if you share the one chosen as the souvenir (with a banner showing the game, the winner and the date), through your phone\u2019s share menu, or in a backup.'],[{bold:'Backing up your data'},': from the settings, the app can create a file containing your players and your games (photos included), your tournaments, your challenges and your settings. You choose where to save or send it (Files, iCloud Drive, Google Drive, email\u2026); that service then applies its own privacy policy. The file is not encrypted: keep it somewhere safe. It is only used to restore your data in Tult, on this phone or another one.'],[{bold:'Review request'},': after a few games, the app may show the App Store or Google Play rating window. If you leave a rating or a review, it is sent to Apple or Google and published under their terms; the app receives nothing from it.']]}]},{title:'Live tournaments',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['With the premium option, a tournament\u2019s organiser can show it on a big screen and let the participants follow it, on tult.app, with the tournament\u2019s code or its QR code. These pages show the tournament\u2019s name, its place if entered, the team and player names, their colours and emojis, the matches, the courts and the scores, never a photo. Anyone who has the code can see them, without an account: only put in names the participants agree to see on display.']},{kind:'paragraph',spans:['On the participants\u2019 page, the team you follow is remembered on your phone, or in your browser on the web. In the app, if you say which of the players you are, the tournament counts in your statistics once it is over.']},{kind:'paragraph',spans:['A live tournament is no longer shown 30 days after its last change. It is erased when the organiser deletes it or deletes their account.']}]},{title:'Tips',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['From the settings, you can leave a tip. The payment is handled entirely by Apple (App Store) or Google (Google Play), under their terms and privacy policy: the app sees neither your name, nor your account, nor your payment details. It only remembers, on your phone, the date of your last tip, to thank you. A tip unlocks no feature and is not a subscription.']}]},{title:'Voice announcements',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['If you turn on voice announcements, the scores are read by the text-to-speech engine built into your phone (iOS or Android). The app does not use the microphone and records no sound.']}]},{title:'Other players',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['If you add people close to you as players, especially with their photo, make sure they agree. Their names, colours and emojis are kept online with your games, and are only visible to the people who played those games, except in a live tournament, which anyone with its code can see. Their photos stay on your phone.']}]},{title:'How long data is kept, and deleting it',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['On your phone, data stays until you delete it. You can delete a game or a tournament from its screen, or by swiping it to the left in the lists. A removed player no longer shows in the lists but stays linked to their past games. To erase everything from the phone, use \xab Erase all data \xbb in the settings, or uninstall the app.']},{kind:'paragraph',spans:['Online, data is kept as long as your account exists. A game you delete is also deleted for the other players; a friend\u2019s game you remove from your statistics only goes for you. To delete your account, open the settings and choose \xab Delete my account \xbb: your profile, profile photo, friend code, friends, players and online games are erased, and the games played with people who have an account stay in their statistics, with no link to you. Uninstalling the app does not delete this online data. You can also ask for deletion from ',{link:'this page',url:o.DELETION_URL_EN},' or by writing to ',{email:o.CONTACT_EMAIL},'.']},{kind:'paragraph',spans:['Your phone\u2019s backups (iCloud or Google) may include the app\u2019s data, depending on your system settings. They then fall under Apple\u2019s or Google\u2019s policy.']}]},{title:'Children',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['The app can be used by the whole family. It asks for no age or real name, and uses no data for advertising. Before linking an account to an email address, a child under 15 needs a parent\u2019s agreement.']}]},{title:'Your rights',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['The General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) gives you a right of access, rectification, erasure, portability and objection. You can view, change, export and delete your information directly in the app, and delete your account in the settings. For any other request, write to ',{email:o.CONTACT_EMAIL},': you will get an answer within one month. You can also lodge a complaint with the ',{link:'CNIL',url:o.CNIL_COMPLAINT_URL},', the French data protection authority.']}]},{title:'Changes',blocks:[{kind:'paragraph',spans:['This policy is updated when the app changes. The current version is always published on this page, with the date it comes into force.']}]}],footer:'Tult \xb7 Privacy policy \xb7 Last updated: 5 November 2026'}},1717,[1598]);
